              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
              which characterizes the based
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            #eq:EvaluationFibrationForLS2.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi ev
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega S^2
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathcal{L}S^2
                    \\xrightarrow{\; ev \;}
                    S^2
            %p
              induces the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              which reads in parts:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mi Ω
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mn 1
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_2(S^2)
                    }}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_1 \Omega S^2
                    }}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\pi_1 \mathcal{L} S^2
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{1}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_1 S^2
                    }}
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              Here,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} homomorphy
              implies that the left map is given by multiplication with some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exactness
              implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_1 \mathcal{L} S^2
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{Z}/n
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+groups"} cyclic groups
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "center center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℚ
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi n
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mtext otherwise,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\mathbb{Z}/n)
                    \\otimes_{{}_{\mathbb{Z}}}
                    \\mathbb{Q}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\begin{array}{ccl}
                    \\mathbb{Q} &amp;\vert&amp; n = 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp;\vert&amp; \text{otherwise,}
                    \\end{array}
                    \\right.
            %p
              comparison with
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RationalFundamentalGroupsOfLS2"} (6)
              implies the first claim
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FundamentalGroupOfLS2"} (4)
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:Integral1HomologyOfLS2"} (5)
              follows by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+theorem"} Hurewicz theorem
              (
              %a{:href => "Hurewicz+theorem#HurewiczTheoremInDegreeOne"}> this Prop.
              ).
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Incidentally, note that the second statement of Cor.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FundamentalGroupAnd1HomologyOfLS2"}
              is compatible with that single generator of degree 1 in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SullivanModelForLS2"} (2)
              being closed, according to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DifferentialInSullivanModelForLS2"} (3)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℒ
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ;
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1(\mathcal{L}S^2; \mathbb{Q}) \simeq \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            Continuing in this manner:
          #SecondHomotopyGroupOfLS2.num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_2 \mathcal{L}S^2
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathbb{Z}^2
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p The argument is analogous to the previous one, so we will be more brief:
            %p
              The relevant part of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              induced by the evaluation fiber sequence
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EvaluationFibrationForLS2"} (7)
              now is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 2
                          %mi Ω
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 0
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mi Ω
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ∼
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mi ℒ
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_3(S^2)
                    }}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_2 \Omega S^2
                    }}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\pi_2 \mathcal{L} S^2
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_2 S^2
                    }}
                    \\xrightarrow{\phantom{-} 0 \phantom{-}}
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_1 \Omega S^2
                    }}
                    \\xrightarrow{\phantom{-} \sim \phantom{-}}
                    \\underset{\mathbb{Z}}{\underbrace{
                    \\pi_1 \mathcal{L} S^2
                    }}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we are using the isomorphism established in the previous corollary. This truncates to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{Z}/n
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\pi_2 \mathcal{L} S^2
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{Z}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    0
            %p
              for some
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_2 \mathcal{L}S^2
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    (\mathbb{Z}/n) \times \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is compatible with the Sullivan model
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SullivanModelForLS2"} (2)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}S^2
              having two generators in degree 2, only if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Of course, the homotopy groups of any free loop space generally follow from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
              induced by the evaluation fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ev
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} X \xrightarrow{ev} X
              using that it has a section
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi const
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \xrightarrow{ const } \mathcal{L}X
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#IteratedLoopSpacesOfNSpheres
            Iterated based loop spaces of
            = succeed "-spheres" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            By iterating the Sullivan model construction for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/based+loop+space"} based loop space
            from Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SullivanModelForBasedLoopSpace"}
            and using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+models+of+n-spheres"} Sullivan models of n-spheres
            we have that:
          #SullivanModelsOfMapsFromSkToSnFornLargerk.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+models"} Sullivan models
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+loop+spaces"} iterated loop spaces
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
              of the
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/iterated+based+loop+space"} iterated based loop space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^k S^n
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \lt n
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mi 𝔩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %mi d
                                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ω
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi n
                                            %mo −
                                            %mi k
                                      %mtd
                                        %mo =
                                        %mn 0
                                %mo )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mtext is odd
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mrow
                                  %mtable
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %mi d
                                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ω
                                          %mrow
                                            %mi n
                                            %mo −
                                            %mi k
                                      %mtd
                                        %mo =
                                        %mn 0
                                    %mtr
                                      %mtd
                                        %mi d
                                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                        %msub
                                          %mi ω
                                          %mrow
                                            %mn 2
                                            %mi n
                                            %mo −
                                            %mn 1
                                            %mo −
                                            %mi k
                                      %mtd
                                        %mo =
                                        %mn 0
                                %mo )
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mtd
                              %mi n
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mtext is even
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mtext for
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE\mathfrak{l}
                    \\big(
                    \\Omega^k S^n
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    d\,\omega_{n-k} &amp; = 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \&amp;\vert&amp;
                    n \;\text{is odd}
                    \\\
                    \\left(
                    \\array{
                    d\,\omega_{n-k} &amp; = 0
                    \\\
                    d\,\omega_{2n-1-k} &amp; = 0
                    }
                    \\right)
                    \&amp;\vert&amp;
                    n \;\text{is even}
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    \\text{for}\; k \lt n
                    \\,.
          %p
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KallelSjerve99"} Kallel-Sjerve 99, Prop. 4.10
          %p
            For the edge case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi D
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^D S^D
            the above formula does not apply, since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{D-1} S^D
            is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            (its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1\big( \Omega^{D-1}S^D \big) = \pi_0 \big(\Omega^D S^D\big) = \pi_D(S^D) = \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} stable homotopy group of spheres
          %p But:
          #RationalModelsForBasedMappingSpaceSDToSD.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The rational model for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^D S^D
              follows from
              %a{:href => "Sullivan+model+of+mapping+space#RationalHomotopyTypeOfMapsNSphereToNsphere"} this Prop.
              by realizing the pointed mapping space as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
